d 'FGCIFPLOT': module to draw Fine-Gray cumulative-incidence plots with conventional and subdistribution risk-set summaries
d
d   fgcifplot draws model-based cumulative-incidence curves after
d Fine-Gray competing-risks regression and can place one or more   
d risk-set summaries below the curve.	 The command distinguishes
d three different quantities that are often conflated in
d competing-risks figures:	  Conventional N at risk: subjects
d whose observed follow-up interval still contains time t. 
d Subjects leave after the event	    of interest, a
d competing event, or censoring.	FG retained N: the
d conventional risk set plus subjects who experienced a competing
d event before t.  Each retained	    competing-event subject
d counts as one.  This is the unweighted head count of the extended
d Fine-Gray risk set.	     FG weighted total: the conventional
d risk set plus retained competing-event subjects weighted by the  
d	   inverse-probability-of-censoring weight used by stcrreg.
d  For a subject j with a prior competing event, the	       
d contribution at time t is the censoring-survival function
d evaluated at t divided by that function evaluated at the	   
d   subject's competing-event time.  This quantity may be
d noninteger.  It is a weighted risk-set total, not a survey-style 
d	    effective sample size.    The cumulative-incidence
d curves are adjusted model predictions produced by stcurve. 
d Covariates not explicitly set in at()    follow stcurve's usual
d postestimation defaults.  In contrast, the risk-set summaries are
d unadjusted observed quantities    calculated within the requested
d groups; they are not model-adjusted predictions. 
d
d KW: graphics
d KW: cumulative-incidence plots
d KW: Fine-Gray
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260917
d
d Author:  Christina Laternser ,  Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children’s Hospital of Chicago
d Support: email christina.laternser.research@@gmail.com
d
f fgcifplot.ado
f fgcifplot.sthlp
f ../d/demo_fgcifplot.do
f ../r/run_fgcifplot_validation.do
f ../s/stress_fgcifplot.do
f ../t/test_fgcifplot.do
f ../t/test_fgcifplot_edgecases.do
f ../t/test_fgcifplot_knowntruth.do
